FIGlet 2.2.5 for OpenVMS
========================

This directory contains FIGlet 2.2.5 for OpenVMS Alpha. This version builds
on OpenVMS only. It uses DCL syntax for its command line. The file README is
the original FIGlet document; where README and this file disagree, this file
is correct.


1. Requirements
---------------
- OpenVMS Alpha 7.0 or later with DEC C, Compaq C, HP C, or VSI C.
- MMS or MMK is optional. BUILD_VMS.COM builds the kit without them.


2. Build and test
-----------------
Copy this directory tree, with [.FONTS] and [.TESTS], to the OpenVMS system.

    $ @BUILD_VMS            ! Build FIGLET.EXE and CHKFONT.EXE
    $ @BUILD_VMS NOTLF      ! Build without TOIlet (.TLF) font support
    $ @BUILD_VMS DEBUG      ! Build with /DEBUG/NOOPTIMIZE
    $ @BUILD_VMS CLEAN      ! Delete the .OBJ and .EXE files

or, with MMS or MMK:

    $ MMS
    $ MMS /MACRO=NOTLF=1
    $ MMS /MACRO=DEBUG=1
    $ MMS CLEAN

Then run the tests:

    $ @TEST_VMS


3. How to run FIGLET
--------------------
FIGLET.EXE is one executable. It needs no setup procedure and no logical
name. It finds its fonts in the [.FONTS] subdirectory of the directory that
contains FIGLET.EXE.

To run it with no setup at all, use MCR with the full file specification:

    $ MCR DKA0:[FIGLET]FIGLET "Hello"

To use the short command FIGLET, do one of these steps. OpenVMS needs one of
them for every program that is not part of the system.

    $ FIGLET :== $DKA0:[FIGLET]FIGLET.EXE       ! a foreign command symbol

    $ DEFINE DCL$PATH DKA0:[FIGLET]             ! or: automatic foreign commands

Put the line in LOGIN.COM (one user) or SYS$MANAGER:SYLOGIN.COM (all users).

Do not use SET COMMAND with FIGLET_CLD.CLD. The command table is inside
FIGLET.EXE.


4. Command syntax
-----------------
    $ FIGLET [qualifiers] ["message"]

If there is no message, FIGLET reads the text from SYS$INPUT (or from the
/INPUT file).

DCL rules apply to the message:
- Text without quotation marks becomes uppercase:  FIGLET Hello  prints HELLO.
- Put the message in quotation marks to keep lowercase letters and spaces.
- To put a quotation mark in the message, type two:  "Say ""Hi""".
- You can give up to 8 words without quotation marks. FIGLET puts one space
  between them.
- Qualifier names and keywords are not case-sensitive. You can abbreviate
  them (4 characters are always sufficient). You do not have to put them in
  quotation marks.

Qualifiers:

    /FONT=name              Font name or file specification. Default: STANDARD.
    /DIRECTORY=dir          Font directory.
    /CONTROL=(file[,...])   Control files (.FLC), applied in the given order.
    /WIDTH=n                Output width in columns. Default: 80.
    /TERMINAL               Use the width of the terminal.
    /JUSTIFY=keyword        LEFT, CENTER, or RIGHT. Default: set by the
                            print direction.
    /RIGHT_TO_LEFT          Print right-to-left.
    /NORIGHT_TO_LEFT        Print left-to-right. Default: set by the font.
    /PARAGRAPH              Paragraph mode: a single newline in the input
                            becomes a space.
    /GERMAN                 Print [ \ ] { | } ~ as German letters.
    /SPACING=keyword        SMUSH, KERN, FULL_WIDTH, or OVERLAP. Default: set
                            by the font.
    /SMUSH_MODE=n           Layout mode number (see FIGFONT.TXT).
    /INPUT=file             Read the text from this file.
    /OUTPUT=file            Write the result to this file.
    /LIST                   List the fonts and control files in the font
                            directory.
    /SAMPLES                Print the message in each font of the font
                            directory. With no message, print each font name.
    /VERSION                Print the version and copyright text.
    /INFO=n                 Print one item: 1 version number, 2 font
                            directory, 3 default font, 4 output width,
                            5 font formats.

You cannot use these qualifiers together: /SPACING with /SMUSH_MODE,
/WIDTH with /TERMINAL, and more than one of /LIST /SAMPLES /VERSION /INFO.

Examples:

    $ FIGLET "Hello, OpenVMS!"
    $ FIGLET /FONT=SLANT /JUSTIFY=CENTER /WIDTH=132 "Hello"
    $ FIGLET /FONT=BANNER /CONTROL=USKATA "ABCDE"
    $ FIGLET /RIGHT_TO_LEFT /FONT=IVRIT "Hello"
    $ FIGLET /INPUT=MESSAGE.TXT /OUTPUT=BANNER.TXT /PARAGRAPH
    $ FIGLET /LIST
    $ FIGLET /SAMPLES /OUTPUT=SAMPLES.TXT "Alpha"

DEFINE/USER_MODE SYS$INPUT, DEFINE/USER_MODE SYS$OUTPUT, and PIPE also
operate.

Old Unix options and the new qualifiers:

    -f font         /FONT=font
    -d dir          /DIRECTORY=dir
    -C file         /CONTROL=file
    -w n            /WIDTH=n
    -t              /TERMINAL
    -l  -c  -r      /JUSTIFY=LEFT  /JUSTIFY=CENTER  /JUSTIFY=RIGHT
    -x              (default; give no /JUSTIFY)
    -R  -L          /RIGHT_TO_LEFT  /NORIGHT_TO_LEFT
    -X              (default; give no /RIGHT_TO_LEFT)
    -p  -n          /PARAGRAPH  (default is no paragraph mode)
    -D  -E          /GERMAN  (default is no German letters)
    -S  -k  -W  -o  /SPACING=SMUSH  =KERN  =FULL_WIDTH  =OVERLAP
    -s              (default; give no /SPACING)
    -m n            /SMUSH_MODE=n
    -v  -I n        /VERSION  /INFO=n
    -N  -A          (not necessary)
    figlist         FIGLET /LIST
    showfigfonts    FIGLET /SAMPLES


5. Font directory
-----------------
FIGLET uses the first of these that applies:

1. The /DIRECTORY qualifier.
2. The logical name FIGLET_FONTS, if it is defined. This is optional.
3. The [.FONTS] subdirectory of the directory that contains FIGLET.EXE.

If /FONT or /CONTROL gives a device or a directory, FIGLET uses that file
specification as it is.

    $ FIGLET /INFO=2        ! shows the font directory in use


6. CHKFONT
----------
CHKFONT.EXE examines font files for format errors. It has file parameters
only and no qualifiers.

    $ MCR DKA0:[FIGLET]CHKFONT DKA0:[FIGLET.FONTS]SLANT.FLF


7. Font file formats
--------------------
- Fonts and control files that are not compressed can have any RMS text
  record format (VAR, VFC, STMLF, STM, STMCR). FIGLET reads them in text
  mode into memory.
- ZIP-compressed fonts are read in binary mode. Transfer them in binary
  mode (for example FTP BINARY).


8. Files
--------
    FIGLET.C          Program. Command line, font directory, /LIST and
                      /SAMPLES use OpenVMS routines (CLI$, LIB$).
    FIGLET_CLD.CLD    DCL command table. SET COMMAND/OBJECT compiles it
                      and LINK puts it in FIGLET.EXE.
    ZIPIO.C INFLATE.C CRC.C UTF8.C   Font file input.
    CHKFONT.C         Font checker.
    BUILD_VMS.COM, DESCRIP.MMS       Build.
    TEST_VMS.COM, [.TESTS]           Tests.
    [.FONTS]          Fonts and control files.

Changes from FIGlet 2.2.5 for Unix:
- DCL command syntax in place of Unix options. getopt is not used.
- The font directory comes from the location of the image.
- figlist and showfigfonts are now FIGLET /LIST and FIGLET /SAMPLES.
- /INPUT and /OUTPUT qualifiers.
- The Unix build files, shell scripts, and man pages are removed.
- The code for other operating systems is removed from FIGLET.C, ZIPIO.C,
  and CHKFONT.C.
